 36AL    9BE(48CA,X):T1/2:XUNDL-2      2023LU07                           202309
 36AL c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2023Lu07:                          
 36AL2c  Phys Rev C 108, 014329 (2023)                                          
 36AL c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), August 08, 2023.                      
 36AL c  2023Lu07: experiments to study decays of {+36}Al and {+36}Mg were      
 36AL2c  carried out at NSCL-MSU, and at FRIB-MSU facilities. At the NSCL-MSU,  
 36AL3c  {+36}Al activity was produced in {+9}Be({+48}Ca,X),E({+48}Ca)=140      
 36AL4c  MeV/nucleon, followed by separation of fragments using A1900 fragment  
 36AL5c  separator. Mixed radioactive beam centered around {+33}Na was          
 36AL6c  delivered to the NSCL |b-decay counting station, where two Si PIN      
 36AL7c  detectors and a scintillator provided the information about the        
 36AL8c  energy loss (|DE) and time-of-flight (tof) for particle identification 
 36AL9c  of the ions. The separated ions were implanted in a CeBr{-3}           
 36ALAc  scintillator detector which was coupled to a position-sensitive        
 36ALBc  photomultiplier tube (PSPMT), and surrounded by the 16 segmented       
 36ALCc  SeGa array of Ge detectors, and 15 LaBr3 detectors. At the FRIB-MSU,   
 36ALDc  {+36}Al activity was produced in {+9}Be({+48}Ca,x),E({+48}Ca)=172.3    
 36ALEc  MeV/nucleon, followed by separation of fragments using the Advanced    
 36ALFc  Rare Isotope Separator (ARIS) separator. Mixed radioactive beam        
 36ALGc  centered around {+42}Si was delivered to the FRIB Decay Station        
 36ALHc  Initiator (FDSi), where two Si PIN detectors and a fast scintillator   
 36ALIc  provided the information about the energy loss (|DE) and time-of-flight
 36ALJc  (tof) for particle identification of the ions. The separated ions      
 36ALKc  were implanted in a YSO scintillator detector which was flanked by two 
 36ALLc  scintillator veto detectors immediately upstream and downstream,       
 36ALMc  and surrounded by 11 HPGe clover detectors and 15 fast-timing LaBr{-3} 
 36ALNc  detectors on one side and the neutron detector array VANDLE on the     
 36ALOc  other side. Measured E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, |g|g-coin, half-lives of the 
 36ALPc  decays of {+36}Mg g.s., {+36}Al g.s. and a newly-discovered isomer.    
 36ALQc  Theoretical calculations of levels, J|p and configurations of {+36}Al  
 36ALRc  and {+36}Si using FSU shell-model Hamiltonians with the CoSMo code.    
 36AL  L  0           (4-)             12.0 MS   20                             
 36AL cL J$From shell-model calculations (2023Lu07)                             
 36AL cL T$Measured by 2023Lu07 from ion-|b-2316|g correlated decay curve.      
 36AL2cL 2023Lu07 also measured T{-1/2}=14.7 ms {I10} from ion-|b correlated    
 36AL3cL decay curve, but adopted T{-1/2}=12.0 ms {I20} due to better           
 36AL4cL channel selectivity through |g-ray detection.                          
                                                                                
